{% extends "tool_layout" %}

{% block tool %}
<section class="alert alert-secondary mt-3" aria-labelledby="strength-heading">
    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
        <h2 class="h4 text-light alert-heading mb-0" id="strength-heading">Check a password</h2>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-dark" data-clear="strength-in" title="Clear" aria-label="Clear">
            <i class="bi bi-hurricane"></i>
        </button>
    </div>
    <hr>
    <div class="input-group">
        <label class="visually-hidden" for="strength-in">Password to check</label>
        <input type="password" class="form-control focus-ring focus-ring-dark" id="strength-in"
            placeholder="Type a password" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary" id="strength-show" title="Show password"
            aria-label="Show password"><i class="bi bi-eye" id="strength-show-icon"></i></button>
    </div>
    <p class="small text-secondary mt-2 mb-0" id="strength-loading">Loading the checker...</p>

    <div id="strength-result" class="mt-3" hidden>
        <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-baseline">
            <strong id="strength-label"></strong>
            <span class="small text-secondary" id="strength-score"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="progress mt-1" role="progressbar" aria-labelledby="strength-label" aria-valuemin="0"
            aria-valuemax="4" id="strength-bar-wrap">
            <div class="progress-bar" id="strength-bar"></div>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-3 mb-1" id="strength-warning" hidden></p>
        <ul class="mb-3 small" id="strength-suggestions"></ul>

        <h3 class="h6 mt-3">Estimated time to crack</h3>
        <table class="table table-sm small mb-0">
            <tbody>
                <tr><td>Online attack, rate-limited (100 guesses/hour)</td><td class="text-end" id="crack-online-throttled"></td></tr>
                <tr><td>Online attack, no rate limit (10 guesses/second)</td><td class="text-end" id="crack-online"></td></tr>
                <tr><td>Stolen database, slow hashing (10,000 guesses/second)</td><td class="text-end" id="crack-offline-slow"></td></tr>
                <tr><td>Stolen database, fast hashing (10 billion guesses/second)</td><td class="text-end" id="crack-offline-fast"></td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>
{% endblock %}

{% block about %}
<h2 class="h4">How strength is measured</h2>
<p>Most strength meters just check for a capital letter, a number and a symbol, which rates
    <code>Password1!</code> as strong. Real attackers don't guess like that: they try common passwords,
    dictionary words, names, dates, keyboard patterns like <code>qwerty</code> and swaps like
    <code>p@ssw0rd</code> first.</p>
<p>This checker uses <a href="https://github.com/zxcvbn-ts/zxcvbn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">zxcvbn-ts</a>,
    which looks for those same patterns, including tens of thousands of common passwords and popular English words,
    names and surnames. It estimates how many guesses a password would take, scores it from 0 to 4, and tells
    you what's weak about it.</p>

<h2 class="h4">What the crack times mean</h2>
<p>The times assume an attacker who knows these tricks. An <strong>online attack</strong> guesses through a
    login page, which is slow, especially when the site limits attempts. A <strong>stolen database</strong>
    lets an attacker guess offline as fast as their hardware allows; how fast depends on how well the site
    stored passwords. Aim for a password that holds up in the "fast hashing" row, because you can't know
    how a site stores yours.</p>

<h2 class="h4">Is it safe to type my password here?</h2>
<p>The check runs entirely in your browser; the password is never sent anywhere or stored. Even so, the
    safest habit is to test passwords that are similar to yours rather than the real thing. For a strong
    password you don't have to think up, use the <a href="/tools/password-generator">password generator</a>.</p>
{% endblock %}
